# worleynoise3d

- Label: Worley Noise 3D
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 32 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/worleynoise3d.html
- Summary (EN): Generates cellular Worley noise from 3D world-space positions. Unlike the 2D Worley Noise COP, which uses image coordinates, each pixel is evaluated at its world position. Output: the noise layer.
- Résumé (FR) : Génère un bruit de Worley 3D évalué aux positions monde de chaque pixel, avec taille de cellule, gigue, métrique et décalage en coordonnées monde.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output image size and metadata", "pos: RGB layer or Vector VDB giving the position at each pixel where the noise is evaluated"]

- Key parameters: ["Element Size: size of the basic noise cell in world coordinates; Per-Component Controls exposes Element Scale for per-axis sizing", "Jitter: random displacement of each grid point before distances are measured; Jitter Scale adds per-axis control", "Metric: Euclidean (circular cells), Manhattan (diamonds), Chebyshev (squares)", "Round Border: smooths the border between cells; appears only when Metric is Euclidean", "Offset: shifts the whole noise field in world coordinates", "Post-processing, applied in order: Complement, Bias, Gain, Gamma, Contrast, Clamp Minimum, Clamp Maximum"]

- Caveats: ["The page warns that values greater than 1 may produce artifacts because they jitter past the search radius, which applies to the Jitter setting"]

